ormat="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOROZUMI, KOICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUI YUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MOROZUMI KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUI, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOROZUMI, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A surface acoustic wave device (1) comprising a substrate (2) composed of quartz, a pair of comb-tooth-shaped electrodes (3) composed of aluminum layers, electrode pads (4) and a pair of lattice-shaped reflectors (5) composed of the same material as that of the electrodes (3). An aluminum layer constituting an electrode (3) has a twin crystal structure, in which, with plane (-11-1) and plane (1-11) of aluminum used as grain boundaries of a twin crystal, a crystal grain involving plane (-111) and plane (002) and a crystal grain involving plane (1-1-1) and plane (00-2) are in a twin crystal relation. Plane {111} of an aluminum layer is oriented at an inclination of 8 DEG  with plane {010} of quartz constituting the substrate (2).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un dispositif à ondes acoustiques de surface (1) comprenant un substrat (2) à quartz, une paire d'électrodes en forme de dents de peigne (3) composées de couches d'aluminium, des plages d'électrodes (4) et une paire de réflecteurs en treillis (5) composés du même matériau que les électrodes (3). Une couche d'aluminium constituant une électrode (3) présente une structure en cristal jumeau, dans laquelle, avec le plan (-11-1) et le plan (1-11) d'aluminium utilisés comme joints de grains d'un cristal jumeau, un grain cristallin comprenant le plan (-111) et le plan (002) et un grain cristallin comprenant le plan (1-1-1) et le plan (00-2) sont en relation de cristal jumeau. Le plan {111} de la couche d'aluminium est orienté selon une inclinaison de 8 DEG  par rapport au plan {010} de quartz constituant le substrat.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>